  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Red Songthaew",
    "overview": "SlipJot is dressed as a Chiang Mai red songthaew, the shared pickup-truck bus. Every slip is a passenger: it climbs on, the route board reads who it paid and how much, and it gets off at its category stop. The truck's materials are the whole vocabulary: body red painted across whole regions, a yellow public-transport licence plate for every amount, double chrome trim between parts of the body, ink-black route-board title strips with white lettering, and the city's real route colours for categories. The display face is Chonburi, the looped heavy Thai sign-painter letter painted on route boards.\n\nThe landing is the side of the truck: full-bleed red, the headline in white and plate yellow, a working route board beside a synthetic slip, chrome trim closing the band. The app is the cabin: a steel-light ground with white route-board panels, a red header strip with chrome trim under it, and the same plate under every total. App screens are calmer than the landing; red narrows to the header, the primary action, charts and over-budget warnings. The world refuses the white-card fintech dashboard and the dark neon crypto look.\n\nLight theme only. There is no dark mode yet; every token here is a light-theme value, and a dark theme would need its own pass rather than inverted tokens. Thai is the first language, so every typographic decision starts from Thai's stacked vowels and tone marks.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Body red owns whole regions; it is a surface, not a sprinkle.",
      "Plate yellow with a warm ink border carries every headline amount, in condensed tabular digits.",
      "Double chrome trim (light line over a dark hairline) divides regions and board rows.",
      "Route boards: white panels with an ink title strip; no nested cards.",
      "Category colours are Chiang Mai's songthaew route colours.",
      "Thai never clips: headings at line-height 1.25 or more, body at 1.6.",
      "Motion is the route board's own: payee writes on, plate digits roll, the stop lights. Everything is visible by default."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Red Owns Regions Rule",
        "body": "Red is painted as whole regions (full-bleed bands, the header strip, a login half) or as the single primary action. It is not used as a scattered accent on app screens.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tinted-On-Red Rule",
        "body": "Text on red is white or rose (on-red-2). Never grey on red.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Plate Rule",
        "body": "A headline amount or total sits on plate yellow with an ink border. Yellow is reserved for amounts, the lit stop, the plate action and focus; it is not a generic highlight.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Clip Rule",
        "body": "Thai stacks marks above and below the line. Headings never go below line-height 1.25 (h1 to h3 default 1.3), body stays at 1.6, and letter-spacing on Thai stays 0.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Whole-Word Break Rule",
        "body": "Thai has no word spaces, so display lines break by hand between whole words: each phrase in a nowrap span, a `<wbr>` where a break is allowed, `<br>` where one is required. Never let the browser break a Thai display line mid-word.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Digits Rule",
        "body": "Every number that can change or be compared is tabular (`.num` or the plate face).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Bolted-On Rule",
        "body": "Shadows sit tight under their object with negative spread; nothing glows and nothing floats in a halo.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do paint red as whole regions (full-bleed bands, the header strip) and close each red band with chrome trim.",
      "Do put every headline amount on a plate: plate yellow, ink double border, Barlow Semi Condensed 600, tabular.",
      "Do use white or rose (#ffd9db) for text on red.",
      "Do title route boards with the ink strip and separate their rows with chrome trim.",
      "Do keep Thai headings at line-height 1.25 or more and body at 1.6, with letter-spacing 0.",
      "Do break Thai display lines by hand between whole words with nowrap spans and `<wbr>`.",
      "Do mark unsure fields with plate wash and a plate-deep border, and label sample data as ข้อมูลสมมติ.",
      "Do keep app screens calmer than the landing: motion only where a number or a read changes."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use grey text on red.",
      "Don't spend plate yellow on decoration; it means an amount, a lit stop, the headline action or focus.",
      "Don't nest boards inside boards.",
      "Don't use emoji as icons; use the single lucide stroke family.",
      "Don't let any element depend on animation to become visible.",
      "Don't ship a raster without recorded provenance, and never a real slip."
